{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2943","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2943","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2943\",\"parent_revision\":\"433712058b23655d8c9bc3c82f0a2e520cf87c88\",\"root_revision\":\"f351c6540157ec24f7e7dd6b7c54b571ea64d8844ac76c31e63beaa4abc0071f\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-08-17\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nRoot `pyproject.toml`'s `[tool.pytest.ini_options] testpaths` includes `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/tests`, but no directory with that path exists anywhere in the current tree (confirmed via `git ls-tree -r HEAD`).\\n\\nDiscovered while adding a drift-guard test comparing `plugins/development-harness/tests/run_pytest.py`'s `_DEFAULT_TEST_PATHS` against `pyproject.toml`'s configured testpaths for that plugin \u2014 the comparison had to explicitly exclude this entry because it points nowhere.\\n\\nImpact: unclear whether this is dead configuration (the directory was removed/renamed and the testpaths entry never cleaned up) or a sign that a set of tests silently stopped being collected at some point. Either way it's stale config that should be corrected \u2014 either restore the missing test directory or remove the entry.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **pyproject.toml testpaths lists plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/tests which does not exist on disk** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 surfaced while adding a pytest config drift-guard test\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added